  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2015-p10.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Adding \\(1\\) to both sides and factoring gives \\[(x+1)(y+1) = 81 = 3^4.\\]\n\nBecause \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) are distinct positive integers with \\(x \\gt y,\\) the only possibility is \\(x+1 = 3^3 = 27\\) and \\(y+1 = 3.\\) Therefore \\(x = 26.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Add \\(1\\) to both sides so the left side factors",
        "\\((x+1)(y+1) = 81;\\) use \\(x \\gt y \\gt 0\\) with \\(81 = 3^4\\)"
      ],
